**Summary:**

I found and fixed an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The bug was that the function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail: `first_word('hello world')` returned `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- `test_single` to error: `first_word('solo')` caused an IndexError because there was no second element

